780
00:38:29,490 --> 00:38:32,390
How can someone feel more confident in meetings?

781
00:38:32,390 --> 00:38:34,190
Preparation is key.

782
00:38:34,190 --> 00:38:35,290
That makes sense.

783
00:38:35,290 --> 00:38:38,490
Before the meeting, think about possible topics.

784
00:38:38,490 --> 00:38:39,990
So you're ready to speak.

785
00:38:39,990 --> 00:38:40,890
Exactly.

786
00:38:40,890 --> 00:38:43,590
Also, practice your sentences out loud.

787
00:38:43,590 --> 00:38:44,990
That helps a lot.

788
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:47,490
Another important thing is mindset.

789
00:38:47,490 --> 00:38:48,490
What do you mean?

790
00:38:48,490 --> 00:38:50,390
Don't try to be perfect.

791
00:38:50,390 --> 00:38:51,830
try to be clear.

792
00:38:51,830 --> 00:38:52,990
That's powerful.

793
00:38:52,990 --> 00:38:55,270
Even native speakers make mistakes.

794
00:38:55,270 --> 00:38:56,950
So mistakes are okay.

795
00:38:56,950 --> 00:38:59,750
Yes, communication is the goal.

796
00:38:59,750 --> 00:39:02,230
Now let's talk about agreeing in meetings.

797
00:39:02,230 --> 00:39:04,750
Yes, this is very important.

798
00:39:04,750 --> 00:39:06,870
How do you agree professionally?

799
00:39:06,870 --> 00:39:09,110
You can say, I agree with you.

800
00:39:09,110 --> 00:39:09,870
Simple.

801
00:39:09,870 --> 00:39:11,870
Or that's a great point.

802
00:39:11,870 --> 00:39:13,110
That sounds natural.

803
00:39:13,110 --> 00:39:15,950
You can also say, I completely agree.

804
00:39:15,950 --> 00:39:16,670
Nice.

805
00:39:16,670 --> 00:39:18,870
If you want to add something, say,

806
00:39:18,870 --> 00:39:20,630
I'd like to build on that.

807
00:39:20,630 --> 00:39:22,150
That's a great phrase.

808
00:39:22,150 --> 00:39:24,790
It shows teamwork and collaboration.

809
00:39:24,790 --> 00:39:26,710
Now what about disagreeing?

810
00:39:26,710 --> 00:39:29,430
This is tricky but important.

811
00:39:29,430 --> 00:39:31,270
Yes, you need to be polite.

812
00:39:31,270 --> 00:39:34,230
Instead of saying, you're wrong, say,

813
00:39:34,230 --> 00:39:36,230
I see your point, but...

814
00:39:36,230 --> 00:39:37,590
That sounds much better.

815
00:39:37,590 --> 00:39:41,350
Or, I understand your perspective, however...

816
00:39:41,350 --> 00:39:42,710
Very professional.

817
00:39:42,710 --> 00:39:44,150
You can also say,

818
00:39:44,150 --> 00:39:46,630
I'm not sure I completely agree.

819
00:39:46,630 --> 00:39:48,390
That's soft and respectful.

820
00:39:48,390 --> 00:39:51,110
Exactly. Let's do a role play.

821
00:39:51,110 --> 00:39:55,350
Great idea. I think we should reduce our budget for advertising.

822
00:39:55,350 --> 00:39:58,550
I see your point, but I have a different opinion.

823
00:39:58,550 --> 00:39:59,910
Okay, tell me more.

824
00:39:59,910 --> 00:40:03,510
I think reducing the budget might affect our visibility.

825
00:40:03,510 --> 00:40:04,870
That's a good point.

826
00:40:04,870 --> 00:40:08,150
Maybe we can optimize instead of reducing.

827
00:40:08,150 --> 00:40:09,590
That sounds reasonable.

828
00:40:09,590 --> 00:40:13,030
Yes, we can focus on high-performing channels.

829
00:40:13,030 --> 00:40:16,390
I agree with that approach. That was a great example.

830
00:40:16,390 --> 00:40:19,670
Yes, and notice how polite the disagreement was.

831
00:40:19,670 --> 00:40:22,150
Now let's talk about asking questions.

832
00:40:22,150 --> 00:40:25,350
Asking questions is a great way to participate.

833
00:40:25,350 --> 00:40:27,590
Yes, even if you don't have an idea.

834
00:40:27,590 --> 00:40:30,230
You can say, could you clarify that?

835
00:40:30,230 --> 00:40:31,270
Very useful.

836
00:40:31,270 --> 00:40:34,230
Or, can you explain that in more detail?

837
00:40:34,230 --> 00:40:34,950
Good one.

838
00:40:34,950 --> 00:40:38,150
Another one is, what do you think about this idea?

839
00:40:38,150 --> 00:40:39,910
That invites discussion.

840
00:40:39,910 --> 00:40:42,390
What if you don't understand something?

841
00:40:42,390 --> 00:40:45,430
You can say, sorry, I didn't catch that.

842
00:40:45,430 --> 00:40:46,750
That's very natural.

843
00:40:46,750 --> 00:40:49,150
Or could you repeat that please?

844
00:40:49,150 --> 00:40:50,750
Simple and effective.

845
00:40:50,750 --> 00:40:54,230
Now let's talk about structuring your ideas.

846
00:40:54,230 --> 00:40:55,950
That's important for clarity.

847
00:40:55,950 --> 00:41:01,270
Yes, use simple structures like first, second, finally.

848
00:41:01,270 --> 00:41:03,350
That helps people follow your idea.

849
00:41:03,350 --> 00:41:07,350
For example, first, we need to analyze the data.

850
00:41:07,350 --> 00:41:10,430
Second, we should identify key trends.

851
00:41:10,430 --> 00:41:12,710
Finally, we can make decisions.

852
00:41:12,710 --> 00:41:14,750
That sounds very clear.

853
00:41:14,750 --> 00:41:16,350
Let's do another role play.

854
00:41:16,350 --> 00:41:17,150
Sure.

855
00:41:17,150 --> 00:41:20,110
What's your opinion on improving team productivity?

856
00:41:20,110 --> 00:41:22,030
I'd like to share my thoughts.

857
00:41:22,030 --> 00:41:22,990
Go ahead.

858
00:41:22,990 --> 00:41:25,710
First, we should improve communication.

859
00:41:25,710 --> 00:41:26,510
Okay.

860
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:29,630
Second, we need better time management tools.

861
00:41:29,630 --> 00:41:30,910
That makes sense.

862
00:41:30,910 --> 00:41:33,790
Finally, we should provide regular feedback.

863
00:41:33,790 --> 00:41:35,230
That's a strong plan.

864
00:41:35,230 --> 00:41:36,830
That was very structured.

865
00:41:36,830 --> 00:41:38,990
Yes, structure builds confidence.

866
00:41:39,630 --> 00:41:42,110
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

867
00:41:42,110 --> 00:41:44,950
Mistake number one, staying silent.

868
00:41:44,950 --> 00:41:46,390
That's the biggest one.

869
00:41:46,390 --> 00:41:48,470
Try to speak at least once.

870
00:41:48,470 --> 00:41:50,830
Mistake number two, overthinking.

871
00:41:50,830 --> 00:41:53,590
Yes, don't overanalyze your grammar.

872
00:41:53,590 --> 00:41:56,510
Mistake number three, speaking too fast.

873
00:41:56,510 --> 00:41:58,590
Slow down and be clear.

874
00:41:58,590 --> 00:42:01,470
Mistake number four, being too negative.

875
00:42:01,470 --> 00:42:04,630
Yes, always be professional and polite.

876
00:42:04,630 --> 00:42:08,230
Let's do one final role play, a real meeting situation.

877
00:42:08,230 --> 00:42:09,350
Perfect.

878
00:42:09,350 --> 00:42:11,470
Let's discuss the project deadline.

879
00:42:11,470 --> 00:42:13,550
I'd like to add something here.

880
00:42:13,550 --> 00:42:14,390
Go ahead.

881
00:42:14,390 --> 00:42:16,910
I think the timeline is too tight.

882
00:42:16,910 --> 00:42:18,110
Why do you think so?

883
00:42:18,110 --> 00:42:20,190
We still need time for testing.

884
00:42:20,190 --> 00:42:21,190
That's true.

885
00:42:21,190 --> 00:42:23,670
I suggest extending the deadline.

886
00:42:23,670 --> 00:42:26,990
I see your point, but the client expects fast delivery.

887
00:42:26,990 --> 00:42:28,630
That's understandable.

888
00:42:28,630 --> 00:42:31,630
Maybe we can prioritize key features.

889
00:42:31,630 --> 00:42:33,190
That's a good compromise.

890
00:42:33,190 --> 00:42:34,070
I agree.

891
00:42:34,070 --> 00:42:35,790
That was very realistic.

892
00:42:35,790 --> 00:42:37,870
Yes, and very useful.

893
00:42:37,870 --> 00:42:39,870
Let's finish with final tips.

894
00:42:39,870 --> 00:42:41,710
Prepare before meetings.

895
00:42:41,710 --> 00:42:43,270
Use simple language.

896
00:42:43,270 --> 00:42:45,070
Speak at least once.

897
00:42:45,070 --> 00:42:46,550
Don't fear mistakes.

898
00:42:46,550 --> 00:42:48,190
Practice regularly.

899
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:50,590
The most important thing is confidence.

900
00:42:50,590 --> 00:42:52,430
Your ideas are valuable.

901
00:42:52,430 --> 00:42:53,910
Your voice matters.

902
00:42:53,910 --> 00:42:56,350
Even if your English is not perfect.

903
00:42:56,350 --> 00:42:57,590
Now it's your turn.

904
00:42:57,590 --> 00:42:59,950
Do you feel confident speaking in meetings?

905
00:42:59,950 --> 00:43:02,070
What phrase will you use next time?

906
00:43:02,070 --> 00:43:03,950
Write your answer and practice.

907
00:43:03,950 --> 00:43:05,750
Thank you so much for watching.

908
00:43:05,750 --> 00:43:07,670
Keep practicing and improving.

909
00:43:07,670 --> 00:43:09,550
We'll see you in the next lesson.

910
00:43:09,550 --> 00:43:10,390
Take care.

911
