in real-life professional situations.

924
00:43:32,030 --> 00:43:33,430
If you enjoy this episode,

925
00:43:33,430 --> 00:43:36,310
don't forget to follow and share it with your friends.

926
00:43:36,310 --> 00:43:38,830
Yes, your support means a lot to us.

927
00:43:38,830 --> 00:43:41,510
So Emily, what are we talking about today?

928
00:43:41,510 --> 00:43:44,950
Today we have a very practical and powerful topic,

929
00:43:44,950 --> 00:43:48,190
how to speak up in business meetings with confidence.

930
00:43:48,190 --> 00:43:50,350
This is such an important skill.

931
00:43:50,350 --> 00:43:51,830
Many people have great ideas,

932
00:43:51,830 --> 00:43:53,710
but they stay silent in meetings

933
00:43:53,710 --> 00:43:56,350
because they feel nervous or unsure.

934
00:43:56,350 --> 00:43:59,790
Exactly, and today we're going to help you change that.

935
00:43:59,790 --> 00:44:02,270
We'll give you useful phrases, strategies,

936
00:44:02,270 --> 00:44:05,510
and real examples so you can speak with confidence.

937
00:44:05,510 --> 00:44:06,510
Sounds great.

938
00:44:06,510 --> 00:44:09,150
So before we start, how are you feeling today?

939
00:44:09,150 --> 00:44:10,270
I'm feeling great.

940
00:44:10,270 --> 00:44:12,110
I'm really excited about this topic

941
00:44:12,110 --> 00:44:14,770
because it can truly change someone's career.

942
00:44:14,770 --> 00:44:15,790
How about you?

943
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:16,990
I'm doing great too.

944
00:44:16,990 --> 00:44:19,550
I think this is something almost everyone struggles with

945
00:44:19,550 --> 00:44:20,670
at some point.

946
00:44:20,670 --> 00:44:21,870
Absolutely.

947
00:44:21,870 --> 00:44:23,870
Okay everyone, let's get started.

948
00:44:23,870 --> 00:44:25,910
Let's begin with a simple question.

949
00:44:25,910 --> 00:44:28,830
Why is it important to speak up in meetings?

950
00:44:28,830 --> 00:44:31,150
Speaking up shows that you are engaged,

951
00:44:31,150 --> 00:44:32,950
confident and professional.

952
00:44:32,950 --> 00:44:36,470
It helps others understand your ideas and your value.

953
00:44:36,470 --> 00:44:41,150
Yes, if you stay silent, people may think you don't have anything to contribute, even

954
00:44:41,150 --> 00:44:42,630
if you actually do.

955
00:44:42,630 --> 00:44:46,990
Exactly, and speaking up can help you build your reputation at work.

956
00:44:46,990 --> 00:44:48,910
But many people feel nervous.

957
00:44:48,910 --> 00:44:50,070
Why is that?

958
00:44:50,070 --> 00:44:51,430
There are many reasons.

959
00:44:51,430 --> 00:44:56,550
Some people are afraid of making mistakes in English, others worry about being judged.

960
00:44:56,550 --> 00:44:59,670
And some people feel their ideas are not good enough.

961
00:44:59,670 --> 00:45:00,670
That's very common.

962
00:45:00,670 --> 00:45:04,990
But remember, you don't need to be perfect, you just need to communicate clearly.

963
00:45:04,990 --> 00:45:06,730
That's such an important point.

964
00:45:06,730 --> 00:45:10,490
Now let's talk about the first step, preparation.

965
00:45:10,490 --> 00:45:11,530
Preparation is key.

966
00:45:11,530 --> 00:45:13,970
When you prepare, you feel more confident.

967
00:45:13,970 --> 00:45:16,470
So what can we do before a meeting?

968
00:45:16,470 --> 00:45:18,230
First, understand the agenda.

969
00:45:18,230 --> 00:45:19,770
What topics will be discussed?

970
00:45:19,770 --> 00:45:22,870
Yes, and think about your ideas in advance.

971
00:45:22,870 --> 00:45:27,170
You can even write down simple sentences like, I'd like to share an idea.

972
00:45:27,170 --> 00:45:28,850
I have a suggestion.

973
00:45:28,850 --> 00:45:30,450
That's a great tip.

974
00:45:30,450 --> 00:45:32,250
Preparation reduces fear.

975
00:45:32,250 --> 00:45:33,250
Exactly.

976
00:45:33,250 --> 00:45:36,610
Now let's talk about how to start speaking in a meeting.

977
00:45:36,610 --> 00:45:38,450
This is often the hardest part.

978
00:45:38,450 --> 00:45:42,550
Yes, but you can use simple phrases like, can I add something?

979
00:45:42,550 --> 00:45:44,330
May I share my thoughts?

980
00:45:44,330 --> 00:45:45,330
Let's practice.

981
00:45:45,330 --> 00:45:46,650
I'll ask a question.

982
00:45:46,650 --> 00:45:49,450
Okay, what do you think about this project?

983
00:45:49,450 --> 00:45:50,650
Can I add something?

984
00:45:50,650 --> 00:45:53,730
I think we should focus more on customer feedback.

985
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:56,610
That was perfect, clear and confident.

986
00:45:56,610 --> 00:45:57,610
Thank you.

987
00:45:57,610 --> 00:46:00,530
Now let's talk about expressing ideas clearly.

988
00:46:00,530 --> 00:46:02,090
Keep your language simple.

989
00:46:02,090 --> 00:46:06,050
Yes, for example, I think this will improve efficiency.

990
00:46:06,050 --> 00:46:08,410
This idea could save time.

991
00:46:08,410 --> 00:46:10,170
Simple is powerful.

992
00:46:10,170 --> 00:46:12,170
Now let's talk about agreeing.

993
00:46:12,170 --> 00:46:14,250
You can say, I agree with you.

994
00:46:14,250 --> 00:46:15,610
That's a good point.

995
00:46:15,610 --> 00:46:20,810
And if you want to add something, I'd like to add to that, building on your idea.

996
00:46:20,810 --> 00:46:21,810
Great.

997
00:46:21,810 --> 00:46:24,010
What about disagreeing politely?

998
00:46:24,010 --> 00:46:25,010
Very important.

999
00:46:25,010 --> 00:46:30,370
You can say, I see your point, but I think I understand, however.

1000
00:46:30,370 --> 00:46:32,770
That sounds respectful and professional.

1001
00:46:32,770 --> 00:46:33,930
Exactly.

1002
00:46:33,930 --> 00:46:35,490
Never say you're wrong.

1003
00:46:35,490 --> 00:46:37,090
That sounds too direct.

1004
00:46:37,090 --> 00:46:38,090
Good advice.

1005
00:46:38,090 --> 00:46:40,570
Now let's talk about asking questions.

1006
00:46:40,570 --> 00:46:42,970
Asking questions shows you are engaged.

1007
00:46:42,970 --> 00:46:45,270
You can say, could you clarify that?

1008
00:46:45,270 --> 00:46:46,770
Can you explain more?

1009
00:46:46,770 --> 00:46:47,770
Perfect.

1010
00:46:47,770 --> 00:46:49,530
Now let's do a role play.

1011
00:46:49,530 --> 00:46:50,530
Great idea.

1012
00:46:50,530 --> 00:46:52,170
Let's imagine a team meeting.

1013
00:46:52,170 --> 00:46:53,170
I'll start.

1014
00:46:53,170 --> 00:46:54,410
Good morning everyone.

1015
00:46:54,410 --> 00:46:56,930
Let's discuss the new marketing strategy.

1016
00:46:56,930 --> 00:46:58,210
Can I share an idea?

1017
00:46:58,210 --> 00:47:01,210
I think we should use more social media advertising.

1018
00:47:01,210 --> 00:47:03,610
That's interesting. Can you explain why?

1019
00:47:03,610 --> 00:47:07,610
Yes, social media allows us to reach a larger audience quickly.

1020
00:47:07,610 --> 00:47:09,710
I agree. That's a good point.

1021
00:47:09,710 --> 00:47:13,010
I'd also like to add that we should track our results carefully.

1022
00:47:13,010 --> 00:47:14,610
Excellent suggestion.

1023
00:47:14,610 --> 00:47:15,410
Thank you.

1024
00:47:15,410 --> 00:47:17,010
That was a great example.

1025
00:47:17,010 --> 00:47:19,510
Yes, very natural conversation.

1026
00:47:19,510 --> 00:47:21,910
Now let's talk about confidence.

1027
00:47:21,910 --> 00:47:24,010
Confidence comes with practice.

1028
00:47:24,010 --> 00:47:26,110
Don't be afraid of mistakes.

1029
00:47:26,110 --> 00:47:27,910
Everyone makes mistakes.

1030
00:47:27,910 --> 00:47:30,690
Focus on your message, not perfection.

1031
00:47:30,690 --> 00:47:32,290
That's very important.

1032
00:47:32,290 --> 00:47:34,690
Now let's share some final tips.

1033
00:47:34,690 --> 00:47:37,290
Tip one, prepare before the meeting.

1034
00:47:37,290 --> 00:47:39,870
Tip two, use simple phrases.

1035
00:47:39,870 --> 00:47:42,770
Tip three, speak clearly and slowly.

1036
00:47:42,770 --> 00:47:45,850
Tip four, don't be afraid to make mistakes.

1037
00:47:45,850 --> 00:47:48,250
Tip five, practice regularly.

1038
00:47:48,250 --> 00:47:49,370
Great tips.

1039
00:47:49,370 --> 00:47:52,070
Now it's time for our question of the day.

1040
00:47:52,070 --> 00:47:55,010
What is the biggest challenge you face in meetings?

1041
00:47:55,010 --> 00:47:57,490
Write your answer and practice your English.

1042
00:47:57,490 --> 00:47:59,370
We love reading your responses.

1043
00:47:59,370 --> 00:48:00,450
Don't be shy.

1044
00:48:00,450 --> 00:48:02,770
Before we finish, thank you for listening.

1045
00:48:02,770 --> 00:48:05,410
Your support means everything to us.

1046
00:48:05,410 --> 00:48:07,810
Keep practicing and stay confident.

1047
00:48:07,810 --> 00:48:09,410
See you in the next episode.

1048
00:48:09,410 --> 00:48:10,330
Goodbye, everyone.
